GURUFLOW — COMPLETE PREMIUM NATIVE MOBILE APPLICATION
MASTER PROMPT: FULL PRODUCT UI, ALL 82 SCREENS & INTERACTIVE PROTOTYPE
You are acting as a world-class product designer, senior React Native engineer, mobile UX architect, design systems engineer, and product prototyping specialist.
Your task is to design and implement the complete user interface of GuruFlow, a premium, India-first institute management and learning application.
This is not a landing page, website, static Figma-style mockup, or collection of disconnected screens.
You must create a real, runnable, native-feeling mobile application with a complete navigation system, realistic demo data, functional interactions, and a consistent premium design system.
The result must look and behave like a polished commercial education technology product that could eventually be released on the Google Play Store.
1. PRODUCT UNDERSTANDING
1.1 What is GuruFlow?
GuruFlow is a complete digital operating system for educational institutes, coaching centres, schools, and tuition organisations.
It connects four major groups:
Institute Owner / Principal / Administrator
Teacher
Student
Parent / Guardian
The institute is the primary paying customer, but the product must provide meaningful daily value to all four groups.
The product should replace fragmented workflows involving paper registers, WhatsApp groups, spreadsheets, fee registers, manual attendance, exam records, and scattered learning resources.
GuruFlow should bring these workflows into one well-organised mobile application.
1.2 Core product philosophy
Design around these principles:
Extremely easy to understand, even for non-technical Indian users.
Premium visual appearance without unnecessary visual complexity.
Fast access to the most important daily tasks.
Clear information hierarchy.
Role-specific experiences.
Meaningful notifications and reminders.
Strong privacy and permission boundaries.
Consistent navigation.
No unnecessary features that make the app confusing.
No artificial engagement tricks or manipulative gamification.
No fake functionality.
The application should feel like a carefully designed premium product, not a generic admin template.
